<!--
  Adds the volunteering opt-in to the new-sponsorship flow. The checkbox ends
  up on res.partner.interested_for_volunteering (partner_compassion), which
  is what notifies the volunteer staff of a potential advocate.

  Target:
  - my_compassion.my2_new_sponsorship_thank_you_page — the public-visitor
    "All set" summary shown once the sponsor's name is in (their placeholder
    partner is replaced, see res.partner._my2_on_placeholder_name_replaced),
    below the child card (standard flow) or the Write&amp;Pray first-timer
    "write your first letter" card (wap-preferences-card) when that one
    renders instead.

  Why there, and not the checkout page or the details form any more:
  the opt-in used to live on the wizard's communication-details step, which
  the fast checkout no longer runs in any flow (see
  new.sponsorship.wizard.STEPS_CONFIGS / _get_step_xmlids: the public flows
  substitute that step, the logged-in flows never listed it). Asking it on
  the checkout page would defeat the point of that page, which is to hold
  nothing but what is needed to pay. It briefly lived on the post-payment
  "Who shall we thank?" details form instead - same audience, moved from
  before the payment to after it - but moved again onto this summary once it
  existed: it reads better as "one more thing you can do" alongside the
  finished sponsorship than as one more required-adjacent field on a form
  whose only two required fields are name and phone.

  This page has no <form> of its own (it is a summary, not a step), so the
  checkbox posts itself via /my2/new-sponsorship/volunteering on change
  (my2_new_sponsorship_wizard_volunteering.js) instead of waiting for a
  submit button - see controllers/my2_sponsorships.py
  ::sponsorship_volunteering_optin for the write and its access gate.

  Consequence, and it is the intended one: the flag arrives in a write to an
  existing partner, which is what finally makes partner_compassion's
  "Potential volunteer" activity fire (it only ever looked at write()). See
  partner_compassion/models/partner_compassion.py.
-->
<odoo>
  <template
    id="new_sponsorship_wizard_volunteering"
    inherit_id="my_compassion.my2_new_sponsorship_thank_you_page"
    name="New Sponsorship All Set Volunteering Opt-in"
  >
    <xpath expr="//div[hasclass('wap-preferences-card')]" position="after">
      <div
        class="w-100 mb-1 mt-3 text-dark-blue body-small bold text-center"
      >Want to do more?</div>
      <div class="my-3">
        <label
          for="all_set_volunteering"
          class="toggle-card w-100 d-flex align-items-center p-3 rounded rounded-lg bg-light-green border border-mid-grey"
        >
          <input
            type="checkbox"
            id="all_set_volunteering"
            class="d-none"
            data-action="volunteering-optin"
            t-att-data-sponsorship-id="sponsorship.id"
            t-att-checked="sponsorship.partner_id.interested_for_volunteering"
          />
          <span
            class="toggle-card-check me-3 flex-shrink-0 d-flex align-items-center justify-content-center rounded-circle bg-mid-green text-pure-white tiny-text bold"
          >✓</span>
          <span class="flex-grow-1">
            <span class="d-block text-dark-blue very-tiny-text bold">Volunteer with us</span>
            <span class="d-block text-mid-grey very-tiny-text">Letter translations, events, prayer, and more.</span>
          </span>
        </label>
        <a
          href="#"
          class="d-inline-block mt-2 very-tiny-text bold text-core-blue"
          data-bs-toggle="modal"
          data-bs-target="#volunteering-info-modal"
        >What could I help with?</a>
      </div>
      <!-- Volunteering info modal -->
      <div
        class="modal fade"
        id="volunteering-info-modal"
        tabindex="-1"
        role="dialog"
        aria-labelledby="volunteering-info-modal-title"
        aria-hidden="true"
      >
        <div class="modal-dialog modal-dialog-centered" role="document">
          <div class="modal-content border-0">
            <div class="modal-body">
              <button
                type="button"
                class="btn-close mt-3 me-3 icon-x-circle body-large text-mid-grey"
                data-bs-dismiss="modal"
                aria-label="Close"
              />
              <div class="px-4 pt-2 pb-4">
                <div
                  id="volunteering-info-modal-title"
                  class="mb-2 text-dark-blue body-large bold"
                >Volunteering for compassion</div>
                <div class="body-small">
                            Do you want to inspire other people to sponsor a child?
                            Does the situation of children in need particularly touch you and you want to take action?
                            <br />
                            <br />
                            You can volunteer for Compassion and thereby place your talents at the service of the most
                            destitute children
                            on the planet.
                            <br />
                            <br />
                            Translations, stuffing envelopes, presence at events, being a spokesperson in
                            your church or running for the children.
                        </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </xpath>
  </template>
</odoo>
